  data: {
    LLM: "When choosing trumps, select the suit in which you have most cards. Between two equal suits, prefer the one without the aceâ€”the ace is likely to win a trick whether trump or not.\n\nRemember what cards have been played. Do not normally beat or trump your partner's winning card. Use discards to signal: if partner leads and you have no cards of that suit, discard from a suit you want led (e.g. your highest or only card of that suit).\n\nFinesse: holding ace and queen of a led suit, play the queen to gain a trick when the opponent to your left has the king. With four cards in four different suits, picking trump is a guess; some players choose the suit of the lowest card.",
